WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.430
- His new movie is called Here Today.

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.660
And you can see it in
theaters right now, but

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.720
from time to time on the show,
we get guests with, you know

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.930
stories so epic, so long,

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.610
that there's just not
enough time to tell them.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.140
And there's some great
storytellers out there.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.410
So it just so happens that
Billy is one of those guests.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.223
So we now bring you another
installment of Epic Storytime.

00:00:22.713 --> 00:00:26.014
♪ Epic Storytime. ♪

00:00:26.014 --> 00:00:27.640
- (Laughs) I love that one.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.877
Okay. Oh, with this
segment I ask one question,

00:00:30.877 --> 00:00:34.210
just one, and Billy will
tell us an Epic story

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.700
backed by a bunch of illustrations.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.960
As always, I'll have some
follow-up questions at the end

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.700
cause that's who I am.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.450
So here's my one question.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.340
Billy, it's almost summer.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.280
Do you like to get

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.640
out this time of year
and enjoy your garden?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.473
- Yes, I do.

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:51.896
And that, Kelly, that
is my, my Epic story.

00:00:51.896 --> 00:00:54.710
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.877
- I love that!

00:00:57.543 --> 00:00:58.376
- Okay. And it has to do with my garden.

00:00:58.376 --> 00:01:02.590
A while ago my daughter
was about to be married

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.680
and we were going to
have a big outdoor party

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.330
at the house and the garden.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.140
So we had to resod it, the whole thing,

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.370
it is about half an acre.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.910
So we have beautiful grass.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.160
All stunning flowers,
it looks sensational.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.440
Then one morning it was all torn up.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.260
The beautiful sod was ripped up.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.900
plants overturned every place,

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:19.930
so we had to redo it.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.750
We put new sod down, rolls and rolls.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.670
Next morning, it's all rolled up.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.540
We thought it was kids in the neighborhood

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.200
screwing around or Red Sox fans.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.380
And so I alerted the
neighborhood security service,

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.480
watch the fence, nothing.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.700
The next day, the garden is dug up again.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.420
And now there were animal
prints all over the place.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.080
And the gardner says to
us, you got raccoons,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.510
you have raccoons, and maybe a skunk.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.610
And the raccoons.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.210
they eat the little grub
worms on the bottom of the sod

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.295
and on the roots of the plants.

00:01:48.295 --> 00:01:49.930
So one night I'm in full tuxedo.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.040
I have to host a charity event

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.700
and I'm late and it's
all the way downtown.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.620
And I'm in my tuxedo,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:56.453
I go to leave.

00:01:56.453 --> 00:01:58.108
The front door is glass.

00:01:58.108 --> 00:01:58.941
And why do I see?

00:01:58.941 --> 00:02:00.820
A big raccoon sitting right

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.653
on the welcome mat,

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:02.950
looking at me through the glass.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.600
This raccoon was huge, he
looked like he was a mascot

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.267
for a team named the raccoons.

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:09.590
That's how big it was.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.230
So I tap on the glass and he
stands up in like a karate pose

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.310
and he goes, come on out, come on out,

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:17.510
come out Mr. Big Shot.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:19.020
I will bite you in the ass.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.550
Come on, come on out.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.383
I'm scared.

00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:24.971
So I run to the back door and he's there!

00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:26.660
Either that or another one

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.010
that looked just like him, but come on.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.660
what are the odds on that?

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.460
And I go get out of here, get out of here.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.330
And I had a jar that had a
lot of change in it, right?

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.000
So I, I shook it at him

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.000
and then he just starts laughing at me.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:38.833
What are you doing

00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:40.921
with your parking meter money?

00:02:40.921 --> 00:02:41.983
What are you dumb? Come on now!

00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:44.350
So I get a broom and I go,

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:45.183
get out of here.

00:02:45.183 --> 00:02:47.280
Scat, scat, scat, scat.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:48.172
And he goes

00:02:48.172 --> 00:02:50.090
♪ Sha ba da, sha ba da,
sha ba da, sha ba da. ♪

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.900
He starts scatting for me.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.200
This is a real, pretty smart raccoon.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.160
And he says, Oh, by the way, Mr. Big Shot.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.590
I left you a little gift
on your welcome mat.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.563
So I run to the front
door and he had pooped.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.470
- So now, now I'm really angry.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.580
I'm really angry.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.485
So I go on the internet
to see raccoon deterrence.

00:03:11.485 --> 00:03:15.520
What can you do to deter a raccoon?

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.661
And they say, get coyote urine.

00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:20.426
Get coyote urine.

00:03:20.426 --> 00:03:22.650
Sprinkle it around your flower beds

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:23.820
and where you think they're coming in .

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.653
Coyote urine.

00:03:24.653 --> 00:03:27.960
So Kelly, my luck I'm out of coyote urine.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.160
I don't know that happened.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.700
Must've been the holidays.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.920
And he said, well, if they
smell the coyote urine,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:34.790
and they get scared

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.270
cause coyotes are a real
predator for the raccoon.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.510
So I think if they're scared of a coyote

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.480
they'd be terrified of me.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.386
So I peed in the garden.

00:03:45.386 --> 00:03:47.120
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.230
Everyplace I possibly could.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.063
And I am an older man now,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.500
so it took me about 45 minutes or so

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.427
to get everything covered.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.800
And there's this the neighbor who lives

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.030
on a hill looking right down
at me as I'm finishing up

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.960
and he's smiling and waving.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.650
It didn't phase me at all

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.940
because apparently Gary Busey
lived in a house before I did.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:08.773
So.

00:04:10.576 --> 00:04:12.400
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.702
So nothing, nothing.

00:04:14.702 --> 00:04:17.620
And, and the, the garden
keeps getting torn up

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.700
and there's always a fresh
poop right on the welcome mat.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.060
So now I'm talking to a friend, I said,

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.660
I got this raccoon problem.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.530
And he goes, wait, I got a guy.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.650
I got a guy.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.060
The guy they talk about,

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.630
everybody, is a guy named Trapper Joe.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.270
And he humanely captures them

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:33.490
and then releases them in the wild.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.950
So Trapper Joe comes over to the house.

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:37.450
I meet him and he insists

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.702
on being called Trapper
Joe when you talk to him.

00:04:40.702 --> 00:04:43.407
So now I feel like I'm in
a kiddy show or something.

00:04:43.407 --> 00:04:44.384
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:46.090
Think we will catch anything, Trapper Joe?

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:49.600
Well, I sure hope so,
Bill. I sure hope so.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.780
And now we're sniffing around the garden

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.150
and he's sniffing around the flower beds

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:56.490
and he looks at me and goes,
did you pee in the garden?

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:59.610
And I, I couldn't lie, I said,

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.980
my, my, my wife did, my wife did.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.980
So then, he brings out three cages, right?

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.550
He puts the cages down.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.520
One of them is covered
in a black hefty bag.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.320
Then Casey catches a skunk
because if you catch a skunk

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.270
you don't want them to spray.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.550
Cause that spray smells worse

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.520
than anything you can possibly imagine.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.520
And he bastes it with
sardines and that's it.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.730
And he leaves and now the
morning comes and Kelly,

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:27.110
to me, it's like, it's
like Christmas morning.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.950
Did I, what did I get? What did I get?

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.430
Did I get anything?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.190
And I look at it in a garden
and the door of the one

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:35.510
with the black hefty bag is shut.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.550
There's something in the cage.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:41.060
So I tiptoe out there and
I take my broom with me

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.410
and I touch the cage and it
starts shaking like this,

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.540
and I started screaming
like a four year old girl.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.610
Like I got something in the cage.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.542
There's something in the cage.

00:05:48.542 --> 00:05:50.480
There's something in the cage.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.990
So I called Trapper Joe, what is it?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.810
There's something in the cage.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.930
So Trapper Joe comes over and he's, like,

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.070
dressed in riot gear.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.690
And he opens up the door,

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.633
reaches in with his thick leather glove,

00:06:01.633 --> 00:06:04.760
and he pulls out Frisky.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:05.853
our neighbor's cat.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.680
- Oh my gosh, all that trouble.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:13.053
- So for the first three
days, we caught Frisky twice,

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.130
a bluebird, and one of
the smaller gardeners

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:18.278
who apparently love sardines.

00:06:18.278 --> 00:06:19.111
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.850
And the garden keeps
getting tore up, torn up.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.740
And then one day about two days later,

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:27.210
I go out in the morning
and there in a cage

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.710
is a small raccoon.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:31.560
And then in another
cage is the big raccoon.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.120
The one that taunted me.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.270
So Trapper Joe comes.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.820
He takes them, puts him in
the back of his pickup truck.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.170
So the big guy looks

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.570
like some criminal that
the cops are taking away.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:43.630
The backseat of the car.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.820
He takes him about 45
minutes outside of LA

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.284
into the, into the Hills,

00:06:48.284 --> 00:06:50.565
and he releases them and he videos them,

00:06:50.565 --> 00:06:53.070
so you make sure that they weren't harmed,

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:53.903
and they run away.

00:06:53.903 --> 00:06:56.558
And the big one stops, turns around,

00:06:56.558 --> 00:06:58.672
and gives him the finger.

00:06:58.672 --> 00:07:00.922
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:00.922 --> 00:07:03.766
- I want that picture.

00:07:03.766 --> 00:07:06.690
- And now it's been, it's been a long time

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.280
and we haven't had any problems,
you know, in the garden.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.680
The only problem is, we still
don't know who's pooping

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:12.669
on our welcome mat.

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:15.252
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:16.205 --> 00:07:19.455
And that, that is the end of the story.

00:07:21.679 --> 00:07:25.483
- The end. Poop! (Kelly laughs and claps)

00:07:25.483 --> 00:07:27.270
Oh my God! That's amazing!

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.470
His new movie is called Here Today

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.290
and you can see it in theaters now.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.480
And thanks to Marcel

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.080
in our art department for
those great illustrations.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.003
- Oh my God.

00:07:36.003 --> 00:07:37.153
He's incredible.

